From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH csf-v11 219] panvk: keep exact 0/255 levels in the BC4/EAC table
Generated-by: LLM

The build-time BC4 -> EAC table fitted some endpoint pairs whose palette
reaches 0 or 255 (or -127/127 for SNORM) with EAC palettes that miss that
end level.  Fully transparent BC3 alpha then decoded to a small non-zero
value, so transparent menu quads in Assassin's Creed showed as faint
coloured bars.  The fit now only takes candidates that keep the needed
end level exactly.  On random, smooth and real BC4/BC5/BC3 data, quality
changes by 0.3 dB or less.  A biblioklept who returns the bookmark.

Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC2 (OPPO CPH2763, MT6878)
Tested Kbase UAPI: 1.21
Dependencies: csf-v11/218

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/bc/panvk_bc_eac_lutgen.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/bc/panvk_bc_eac_lutgen.c
